# Cloudflare Workers Assets: what NOT to upload from the assets directory.
#
# The assets directory is the repo root, so without this file Wrangler
# uploads everything it finds there. On Cloudflare's builder that includes
# the node_modules it installs for Wrangler itself, and workerd inside it
# is 144 MiB, well past the 25 MiB per-asset limit. That is what made the
# deploy fail with "Asset too large".
#
# _headers and _redirects are deliberately absent from this list: Workers
# Assets reads them for routing and does not serve them as files.

# Build-time dependencies. The site itself has none.
node_modules

# The collected output of `npm run build:dist`. Copying it into itself, or
# uploading it alongside the files it already contains, doubles the deploy.
dist

# ---- Internal dotfiles: repo plumbing, never part of the site ----
# A deploy uploaded .gitignore to production and it was downloadable at
# https://www.wallasstream.com/.gitignore. No key leaked, but it names the
# files that hold them, and none of this is content the site serves.
#
# NOT WRITTEN AS A BLANKET "ANYTHING STARTING WITH A DOT". .well-known is a
# dotted directory that MUST be served: it carries the
# apple-app-site-association file, and dropping it silently breaks the app
# handoff from the site. The matcher in build.mjs has no negation, so a
# catch-all pattern could not spare it. Hence the explicit list.
.DS_Store
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.gitmodules
.assetsignore
.editorconfig
.npmrc
.nvmrc
.node-version
.tool-versions
.prettierrc*
.eslintrc*
.github
.vscode
.idea

# Credentials and local tooling
.env*
.claude
.agents
.wrangler
skills-lock.json

# Source files that produce the site but are not part of it
build.mjs
package.json
package-lock.json
partials
REDESIGN-PLAN.md

# Pages compiles functions/ into the /api routes and does not serve it as
# files. Listing it here only stops the source being uploaded alongside.
# Now inert either way: a Worker with assets never reads this directory.
functions

# THE WORKER'S OWN SOURCE. This is code that runs, not a file the site
# serves, and it must never be uploaded as an asset: at dist/worker/ it
# would be publicly downloadable, and anything under /api/ in the assets
# would shadow the endpoint the Mac app calls. Wrangler bundles main from
# the repo, not from the assets directory, so excluding it costs nothing.
worker
wrangler.jsonc

# Local secrets for `wrangler dev`. Never uploaded, never committed.
.dev.vars*

# Local review artifacts and design benches
_archive
_*.html
*-bench.html
*-prototype.html
usb-diagram.html
wifi-diagram.html
favicons/_originales

# Working masters and source imagery the site does not serve
assets/references
assets/use-case-visuals/*.png
assets/hero-cinematic/hero-master.mp4
assets/hero-cinematic/hero-cine-corrected.mov
assets/hero-cinematic/Orange_*.mp4
assets/hero-cinematic/frames
assets/hero-cinematic/refs
assets/hero-cinematic/cp
